/E (A UDP transmission relies on exact socket endpoints defined by a target IP address and Port number \(e.g., 192.168.1.50:4210\) rather than HTTP URL paths. Unlike streaming protocols, UDP preserves distinct packet boundaries, so client transmissions should format payloads clearly or include explicit string delimiters \(such as \\n or a null terminator \\0\) to allow the receiver to cleanly parse the incoming buffer. )
